/-!
# Subspace topology of rational evaluation points on the closed unit polydisc

Let `K` be a complete ultrametric normed field and `D^n = closedPolydisc n K` the closed unit
polydisc `Spa (K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩, K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩°)`. Each tuple `a` of power-bounded elements of `K`
(equivalently `‖a i‖ ≤ 1` for all `i`) and base point `x : Spa (K, K°)` defines the classical
evaluation point `classicalPoint x a.1 a.2 : D^n` sending `f` to `|f(a)|`.

This file identifies the topology that `D^n` induces on the set of classical evaluation points:

* Over every complete ultrametric normed field `K`, for each fixed series `f ∈ K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩` the
  evaluation map `a ↦ f(a)` is continuous on `{a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}`, and so
  is the parametrization `a ↦ classicalPoint x a.1 a.2` into `D^n`.
* When `K` is nontrivially normed, `a ↦ classicalPoint x a.1 a.2` is a topological embedding: a
  coordinate ball `‖b i - a i‖ ≤ ‖c‖` is cut out by the basic open sets
  `|Tᵢ - aᵢ| ≤ |c| ≠ 0` for a nonzero scalar `c ∈ K` of small norm. Consequently the parametrization
  induces a homeomorphism `classicalPointHomeomorph` onto its range in `D^n`. Nontriviality of the
  norm is essential here: over an infinite trivially normed field with `n ≥ 1`, the metric on
  `(K°)ⁿ = Kⁿ` is discrete while the subspace topology inherited from `D^n` is coarser.
* Because `(K°)ⁿ` is a closed subset of the complete metric space `Kⁿ`, it is complete and
  completely metrizable, hence a Baire space; `classicalPointHomeomorph` transfers `BaireSpace` to
  the subspace of classical evaluation points inside `D^n`.
* In arbitrary dimension `n`, the kernel of evaluation at `a` is generated by the linear polynomials
  `Tᵢ - aᵢ`, so a point of `D^n` whose support contains every `Tᵢ - aᵢ` is `classicalPoint x a ha`.
  When `K°` is compact (for instance when `K` is proper, such as `ℚ_[p]` or a finite extension),
  compactness reduces the separation of any non-classical point from `(K°)ⁿ` to finitely many basic
  opens, showing that the range of `classicalPoint` is closed in `D^n`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph`: the coordinatewise homeomorphism
  `{a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ≃ₜ (Fin n → powerBoundedSubring K)`.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.classicalPointHomeomorph`: over a complete nontrivially normed
  ultrametric field `K`, the homeomorphism from `{a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}` onto
  its range in `closedPolydisc n K`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.evalAtHom_eq_restrictedEval₂` and
  `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.norm_evalAtHom_le`: Huber evaluation on `K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩` agrees with
  Gauss-normed evaluation `MvPowerSeries.restrictedEval₂` and is `1`-bounded for the Gauss norm.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.continuous_evalAtHom_point` and
  `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.continuous_classicalPoint`: continuity of `a ↦ f(a)` and of
  `a ↦ classicalPoint x a.1 a.2`.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isInducing_classicalPoint` and
  `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isEmbedding_classicalPoint`: over a complete nontrivially normed
  ultrametric field, `a ↦ classicalPoint x a.1 a.2` is a topological embedding.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.baireSpace_range_classicalPoint`: the range of `classicalPoint` in
  `closedPolydisc n K` is a Baire space in its subspace topology.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.ker_evalAtHom_eq_span_range_weightedX_sub_weightedC` and
  `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.eq_classicalPoint_of_forall_weightedX_sub_weightedC_mem_supp`:
  multivariable remainder characterization of classical points in `closedPolydisc n K`.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isClosed_range_classicalPoint_of_compactSpace` and
  `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isClosed_range_classicalPoint_of_properSpace`: when `K°` is compact
  (in particular when `K` is proper), the range of `classicalPoint` is closed in
  `closedPolydisc n K`.

## References

* B. Bhatt and D. Hansen, *The six functors for Zariski-constructible sheaves in rigid geometry*,
  Compositio Math. 158 (2022), 437–482; arXiv:2101.09759v2, Example 2.1.
* S. Howe and C. Klevdal, *Admissible pairs and p-adic Hodge structures II: The bi-analytic
  Ax–Lindemann theorem*, arXiv:2308.11064v2, §9.3.
* T. Wedhorn, *Adic Spaces*, arXiv:1910.05934v1, Proposition 5.50 and Example 7.57.
-/

public section

open Filter Topology

namespace TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum

open TauCeti.Huber

section Tuples

variable {n : ℕ} {K : Type*} [NormedField K]

/-- The set of power-bounded tuples in `Fin n → K` is closed, being the product of closed unit
balls. -/
theorem isClosed_setOf_forall_isPowerBounded :
    IsClosed {a : Fin n → K | ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} := by
  have heq : {a : Fin n → K | ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} =
      ⋂ i : Fin n, (fun a : Fin n → K ↦ a i) ⁻¹' Metric.closedBall 0 1 := by
    ext a
    simp [isPowerBounded_iff_norm_le_one]
  rw [heq]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun i ↦ Metric.isClosed_closedBall.preimage (continuous_apply i)

/-- Over a complete normed field `K`, the space of power-bounded tuples in `Fin n → K` is
complete. -/
instance instCompleteSpaceSubtypeForallIsPowerBounded [CompleteSpace K] :
    CompleteSpace {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} :=
  IsComplete.completeSpace_coe (s := {a : Fin n → K | ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)})
    isClosed_setOf_forall_isPowerBounded.isComplete

variable [IsUltrametricDist K]

variable (n K) in
/-- Coordinatewise homeomorphism between `{a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}` and
`Fin n → powerBoundedSubring K`. -/
def powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph :
    {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ≃ₜ (Fin n → powerBoundedSubring K) where
  toFun a i := ⟨a.1 i, mem_powerBoundedSubring.mpr (a.2 i)⟩
  invFun b := ⟨fun i ↦ (b i : K), fun i ↦ mem_powerBoundedSubring.mp (b i).2⟩
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv _ := rfl
  continuous_toFun :=
    continuous_pi fun i ↦ ((continuous_apply i).comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _
  continuous_invFun :=
    (continuous_pi fun i ↦ continuous_subtype_val.comp (continuous_apply i)).subtype_mk _

@[simp]
theorem powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph_apply_coe
    (a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}) (i : Fin n) :
    (powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph n K a i : K) = a.1 i :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph_symm_apply_coe
    (b : Fin n → powerBoundedSubring K) (i : Fin n) :
    ((powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph n K).symm b).1 i = (b i : K) :=
  (rfl)

end Tuples

section Continuity

variable {n : ℕ} {K : Type*} [NormedField K] [IsUltrametricDist K] [CompleteSpace K]

/-- **Huber evaluation on `K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩` agrees with Gauss-normed evaluation.** Both are continuous
ring homomorphisms fixing constants and sending `Tᵢ` to `aᵢ`. -/
theorem evalAtHom_eq_restrictedEval₂ (a : Fin n → K) (ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i))
    (f : weightedRestrictedSubring (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight) :
    evalAtHom a ha f =
      MvPowerSeries.restrictedEval₂ (RingHom.id K) a (fun _ ↦ le_rfl)
        (fun i ↦ isPowerBounded_iff_norm_le_one.mp (ha i))
        (restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv f) := by
  have heq : (evalAtHom a ha).comp (restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv (n := n) (R := K)).symm =
      MvPowerSeries.restrictedEval₂ (RingHom.id K) a (fun _ ↦ le_rfl)
        (fun i ↦ isPowerBounded_iff_norm_le_one.mp (ha i)) := by
    refine MvPowerSeries.eq_restrictedEval₂ (RingHom.id K) a (fun _ ↦ le_rfl) _ _
      ((continuous_evalAtHom a ha).comp continuous_restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv_symm)
      (fun r ↦ ?_) (fun i ↦ ?_)
    · have hc : (restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv (n := n) (R := K)).symm (algebraMap K _ r) =
          weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight r :=
        restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv.injective (by simp)
      simp [hc]
    · have hx : (restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv (n := n) (R := K)).symm
          ⟨MvPowerSeries.X i, MvPowerSeries.isRestricted_monomial _ (Finsupp.single i 1) 1⟩ =
          weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight i :=
        restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv.injective (by ext; simp)
      simp [hx]
  simpa using RingHom.congr_fun heq (restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv f)

/-- Evaluating `f ∈ K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩` at a power-bounded tuple does not increase its Gauss norm. -/
theorem norm_evalAtHom_le (a : Fin n → K) (ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i))
    (f : weightedRestrictedSubring (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight) :
    ‖evalAtHom a ha f‖ ≤ ‖restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv f‖ := by
  rw [evalAtHom_eq_restrictedEval₂]
  exact MvPowerSeries.norm_restrictedEval₂_le _ _ _ _ _

/-- **For each fixed `f ∈ K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩`, the evaluation map `a ↦ f(a)` is continuous** on the space
of power-bounded tuples. Polynomials are continuous by `MvPolynomial.continuous_eval` and uniformly
approximate `f` in the Gauss norm. -/
theorem continuous_evalAtHom_point
    (f : weightedRestrictedSubring (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight) :
    Continuous fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦ evalAtHom a.1 a.2 f := by
  rw [Metric.continuous_iff]
  intro a ε hε
  set F := restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv f
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := Metric.mem_closure_range_iff.mp
    (TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.denseRange_polynomialToRestricted (R := K)
      (c := fun _ : Fin n ↦ (1 : ℝ)) F) ε hε
  set P := TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.polynomialToRestricted (R := K) (fun _ : Fin n ↦ (1 : ℝ)) p
  have hp' : ‖F - P‖ < ε := by simpa [P, dist_eq_norm] using hp
  have hcont : Continuous fun b : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      MvPolynomial.eval b.1 p :=
    (MvPolynomial.continuous_eval p).comp continuous_subtype_val
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, hball⟩ := Metric.continuousAt_iff.mp hcont.continuousAt ε hε
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, fun b hb ↦ ?_⟩
  have hev (q : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}) :
      MvPowerSeries.restrictedEval₂ (RingHom.id K) q.1 (fun _ ↦ le_rfl)
          (fun i ↦ isPowerBounded_iff_norm_le_one.mp (q.2 i)) P =
        MvPolynomial.eval q.1 p := by
    simp [P, TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.polynomialToRestricted_apply, MvPolynomial.eval₂_id]
  have hrem (q : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}) :
      ‖evalAtHom q.1 q.2 f - MvPolynomial.eval q.1 p‖ < ε := by
    rw [evalAtHom_eq_restrictedEval₂, ← hev q, ← map_sub]
    exact (MvPowerSeries.norm_restrictedEval₂_le _ _ _ _ (F - P)).trans_lt hp'
  have hsplit : evalAtHom b.1 b.2 f - evalAtHom a.1 a.2 f =
      ((evalAtHom b.1 b.2 f - MvPolynomial.eval b.1 p) +
        (MvPolynomial.eval b.1 p - MvPolynomial.eval a.1 p)) +
        -(evalAtHom a.1 a.2 f - MvPolynomial.eval a.1 p) := by
    ring
  rw [dist_eq_norm, hsplit]
  refine (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans_lt
    (max_lt ?_ (by rw [norm_neg]; exact hrem a))
  refine (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans_lt (max_lt (hrem b) ?_)
  simpa [dist_eq_norm] using hball hb

/-- **The classical-point parametrization `(K°)ⁿ → closedPolydisc n K` is continuous** over every
complete ultrametric normed field `K`. -/
theorem continuous_classicalPoint (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    Continuous fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      classicalPoint x a.1 a.2 := by
  refine Topology.IsInducing.subtypeVal.continuous_iff.mpr ?_
  rw [instTopologicalSpace_eq_generateFrom, continuous_generateFrom_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨f, g, rfl⟩
  rw [isOpen_iff_mem_nhds]
  intro a ha
  simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Function.comp_apply, mem_basicOpen_iff, classicalPoint_vle,
    map_zero, vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2, norm_zero, norm_le_zero_iff] at ha
  have hga : 0 < ‖evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr ha.2
  have hU : ∀ᶠ b : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} in 𝓝 a,
      ‖evalAtHom b.1 b.2 f - evalAtHom a.1 a.2 f‖ < ‖evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g‖ ∧
        ‖evalAtHom b.1 b.2 g - evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g‖ < ‖evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g‖ := by
    refine (((continuous_evalAtHom_point f).tendsto a).eventually
      (Metric.ball_mem_nhds _ hga)).and (((continuous_evalAtHom_point g).tendsto a).eventually
        (Metric.ball_mem_nhds _ hga)) |>.mono ?_
    rintro b ⟨hbf, hbg⟩
    simpa only [Metric.mem_ball, dist_eq_norm] using And.intro hbf hbg
  refine hU.mono fun b ⟨hbf, hbg⟩ ↦ ?_
  simp only [Function.comp_apply, mem_basicOpen_iff, classicalPoint_vle, map_zero,
    vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2, norm_zero, norm_le_zero_iff]
  have hgb_eq : ‖evalAtHom b.1 b.2 g‖ = ‖evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g‖ := by
    have hadd : evalAtHom b.1 b.2 g =
        (evalAtHom b.1 b.2 g - evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g) + evalAtHom a.1 a.2 g := by ring
    rw [hadd, IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_eq_max_of_norm_ne_norm hbg.ne, max_eq_right hbg.le]
  refine ⟨?_, norm_pos_iff.mp (hgb_eq ▸ hga)⟩
  have hadd : evalAtHom b.1 b.2 f =
      (evalAtHom b.1 b.2 f - evalAtHom a.1 a.2 f) + evalAtHom a.1 a.2 f := by ring
  rw [hgb_eq, hadd]
  exact (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans (max_le hbf.le ha.1)

/-! ### Multivariable remainder characterization of classical points -/

/-- **Multivariable remainder membership in `K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩`.** Over a complete ultrametric normed
field `K`, for every `a ∈ (K°)ⁿ` and `f ∈ K⟨T₁, …, Tₙ⟩`, the difference `f - f(a)` belongs to the
ideal generated by `T₀ - a₀, …, Tₙ₋₁ - aₙ₋₁`. The ideal is closed on the Gauss-normed side and
contains `p - p(a)` for every polynomial `p`, which is dense. -/
theorem sub_weightedC_evalAtHom_mem_span_range (a : Fin n → K) (ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i))
    (f : weightedRestrictedSubring (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight) :
    f - weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (evalAtHom a ha f) ∈
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦
        weightedX (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
          weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i)) := by
  let T := MvPowerSeries.IsRestricted.subring (R := K) (fun _ : Fin n ↦ (1 : ℝ))
  let e := restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv (n := n) (R := K)
  let I := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦
    weightedX (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
      weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i))
  let J : Ideal T := I.map e.toRingHom
  have hJclosed : IsClosed (J : Set T) := TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.isClosed_ideal_isRestrictedSubring J
  let ha' : ∀ i, ‖a i‖ ≤ (1 : ℝ) := fun i ↦ isPowerBounded_iff_norm_le_one.mp (ha i)
  let ev : T →+* K := MvPowerSeries.restrictedEval₂ (RingHom.id K) a (fun _ ↦ le_rfl) ha'
  have hΦcont : Continuous (fun g : T ↦ g - algebraMap K T (ev g)) :=
    continuous_id.sub (MvPowerSeries.isometry_algebraMap_isRestrictedSubring.continuous.comp
      (MvPowerSeries.continuous_restrictedEval₂ (RingHom.id K) a (fun _ ↦ le_rfl) ha'))
  have hpoly : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) K,
      (fun g : T ↦ g - algebraMap K T (ev g))
          (TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.polynomialToRestricted (fun _ : Fin n ↦ (1 : ℝ)) p) ∈ J := by
    have hhom : (Ideal.Quotient.mk J).comp
        (TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.polynomialToRestricted (R := K)
          (fun _ : Fin n ↦ (1 : ℝ))).toRingHom =
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk J).comp ((algebraMap K T).comp (MvPolynomial.eval a)) := by
      apply MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext
      · intro r
        simp [T]
      · intro i
        simp only [RingHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, AlgHom.coe_toRingHom,
          MvPolynomial.eval_X, Ideal.Quotient.eq]
        have hxi : TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.polynomialToRestricted (fun _ : Fin n ↦ (1 : ℝ))
              (MvPolynomial.X i) - algebraMap K T (a i) =
            e (weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
              weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i)) :=
          Subtype.ext (by simp [e, T])
        rw [hxi]
        exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem e.toRingHom (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
    intro p
    rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, map_sub, sub_eq_zero]
    simpa [T, ev, TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.polynomialToRestricted_apply, MvPolynomial.eval₂_id] using
      RingHom.congr_fun hhom p
  have hmemJ : e f - algebraMap K T (ev (e f)) ∈ J := by
    have hclosed : IsClosed {g : T | g - algebraMap K T (ev g) ∈ J} :=
      hJclosed.preimage hΦcont
    exact hclosed.closure_subset_iff.mpr (Set.range_subset_iff.mpr hpoly)
      (TauCeti.MvPowerSeries.denseRange_polynomialToRestricted (e f))
  have himg : e (f - weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (evalAtHom a ha f)) =
      e f - algebraMap K T (ev (e f)) := by
    rw [map_sub, evalAtHom_eq_restrictedEval₂]
    exact congrArg (e f - ·) (restrictedMvPowerSeriesGaussEquiv_weightedC _)
  have hcomap : I.comap e.symm.toRingHom = J := by
    rw [RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe, Ideal.comap_coe, Ideal.comap_symm]
    rfl
  rw [← himg, ← hcomap] at hmemJ
  simpa using hmemJ

/-- **The kernel of evaluation at `a ∈ (K°)ⁿ` is generated by `T₀ - a₀, …, Tₙ₋₁ - aₙ₋₁`.** -/
theorem ker_evalAtHom_eq_span_range_weightedX_sub_weightedC
    (a : Fin n → K) (ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)) :
    RingHom.ker (evalAtHom a ha) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦
        weightedX (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
          weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i)) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun f hf ↦ ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · have h := sub_weightedC_evalAtHom_mem_span_range a ha f
    rwa [RingHom.mem_ker.mp hf, map_zero, sub_zero] at h
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    simp

/-- **The support of `classicalPoint x a ha` is generated by `T₀ - a₀, …, Tₙ₋₁ - aₙ₋₁`.** -/
theorem supp_classicalPoint_eq_span_range_weightedX_sub_weightedC
    (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) (a : Fin n → K) (ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)) :
    (classicalPoint x a ha).1.supp =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦
        weightedX (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
          weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i)) := by
  rw [← ker_evalAtHom_eq_span_range_weightedX_sub_weightedC a ha]
  ext f
  rw [mem_supp_iff, classicalPoint_vle, map_zero, vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2, norm_zero,
    norm_le_zero_iff, RingHom.mem_ker]

/-- **A point of `closedPolydisc n K` whose support contains every `Tᵢ - aᵢ` is the classical point
at `a`.** -/
theorem eq_classicalPoint_of_forall_weightedX_sub_weightedC_mem_supp (v : closedPolydisc n K)
    (a : Fin n → K) (ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i))
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight i - weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i) ∈
        v.1.supp)
    (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) : v = classicalPoint x a ha := by
  have hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦
      weightedX (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
        weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i)) ≤ v.1.supp :=
    Ideal.span_le.mpr <| Set.range_subset_iff.mpr hv
  have hval (f : weightedRestrictedSubring (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K))
      isWeightFamily_one_weight) :
      v.1.valuation f =
        v.1.valuation (weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (evalAtHom a ha f)) := by
    have hmem : f - weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (evalAtHom a ha f) ∈
        v.1.valuation.supp :=
      supp_eq_valuation_supp v.1 ▸ hspan (sub_weightedC_evalAtHom_mem_span_range a ha f)
    conv_lhs => rw [← sub_add_cancel f (weightedC _ _ (evalAtHom a ha f)), add_comm]
    exact Valuation.map_add_supp _ _ hmem
  refine Subtype.ext (ext' fun f g ↦ ?_)
  rw [classicalPoint_vle, vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2, ← closedPolydisc_vle_weightedC_iff v,
    ← valuation_le_iff, ← valuation_le_iff, hval f, hval g]

/-- Any point `v` of `closedPolydisc n K` distinct from `classicalPoint x a ha` is separated from
`a` by a basic open `|ϖᵐ| ≤ |Tᵢ - aᵢ| ≠ 0` for any topologically nilpotent scalar `ϖ ∈ K`. -/
theorem exists_mem_basicOpen_weightedX_sub_weightedC_of_ne_classicalPoint
    {v : closedPolydisc n K} {x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)}
    {a : Fin n → K} {ha : ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} (hne : v ≠ classicalPoint x a ha)
    {ϖ : K} (hϖ : IsTopologicallyNilpotent ϖ) :
    ∃ (i : Fin n) (m : ℕ),
      v.1 ∈ basicOpen (weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (ϖ ^ m))
        (weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
          weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i)) := by
  have hnil : IsTopologicallyNilpotent
      (weightedC (fun _ : Fin n ↦ ({1} : Set K)) isWeightFamily_one_weight ϖ) :=
    hϖ.map (continuous_weightedC isWeightFamily_one_weight)
  have hcont := ((mem_closedPolydisc_iff n K v.1).mp v.2).1
  have hnot : ¬ ∀ i : Fin n,
      weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight i - weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a i) ∈
        v.1.supp :=
    fun hall ↦ hne (eq_classicalPoint_of_forall_weightedX_sub_weightedC_mem_supp v a ha hall x)
  push Not at hnot
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hnot
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := IsContinuous.exists_pow_vlt_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent hcont hnil hi
  refine ⟨i, m, ?_⟩
  rw [mem_basicOpen_iff, map_pow]
  exact ⟨(valuation_le_iff v.1 _ _).mp ((valuation_lt_iff v.1 _ _).mpr hm).le,
    fun h0 ↦ hi ((mem_supp_iff _ _).mpr h0)⟩

end Continuity

section Embedding

variable {n : ℕ} {K : Type*} [NontriviallyNormedField K] [IsUltrametricDist K] [CompleteSpace K]

/-- **Over a complete nontrivially normed ultrametric field `K`, the classical-point map induces
the product norm topology on `(K°)ⁿ`.** Coordinate balls around `a` are cut out by the basic opens
`|Tᵢ - aᵢ| ≤ |c| ≠ 0` for scalars `c ∈ K` of small positive norm. -/
theorem isInducing_classicalPoint (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    Topology.IsInducing fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      classicalPoint x a.1 a.2 := by
  rw [Topology.isInducing_iff_nhds]
  intro a
  refine le_antisymm ((continuous_classicalPoint x).tendsto a).le_comap ?_
  rw [Metric.nhds_basis_ball.ge_iff]
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨c, hc₀, hcε⟩ := NormedField.exists_norm_lt K hε
  have hc_ne : c ≠ 0 := norm_pos_iff.mp hc₀
  let V : Set (closedPolydisc n K) :=
    ⋂ i : Fin n, Subtype.val ⁻¹'
      basicOpen (weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight i -
          weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a.1 i))
        (weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight c)
  have hVopen : IsOpen V :=
    isOpen_iInter_of_finite fun i ↦ (isOpen_basicOpen _ _).preimage continuous_subtype_val
  have haV : classicalPoint x a.1 a.2 ∈ V := by
    refine Set.mem_iInter.mpr fun i ↦ ?_
    simp [mem_basicOpen_iff, classicalPoint_vle, vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2, hc_ne]
  refine Filter.mem_of_superset (Filter.preimage_mem_comap (hVopen.mem_nhds haV)) fun b hb ↦ ?_
  rw [Metric.mem_ball, Subtype.dist_eq, dist_pi_lt_iff hε]
  intro i
  have hbi := Set.mem_iInter.mp hb i
  simp only [Set.mem_preimage, mem_basicOpen_iff, classicalPoint_vle, map_sub, map_zero,
    evalAtHom_weightedX, evalAtHom_weightedC, vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2] at hbi
  rw [dist_eq_norm]
  exact hbi.1.trans_lt hcε

/-- **Over a complete nontrivially normed ultrametric field `K`, `a ↦ classicalPoint x a.1 a.2` is a
topological embedding** into `closedPolydisc n K`. -/
theorem isEmbedding_classicalPoint (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    Topology.IsEmbedding fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      classicalPoint x a.1 a.2 :=
  ⟨isInducing_classicalPoint x, classicalPoint_injective_of_isField (Field.toIsField K) x⟩

/-- **Homeomorphism between `(K°)ⁿ` and the subspace of classical evaluation points** in
`closedPolydisc n K` over a complete nontrivially normed ultrametric field `K`. -/
noncomputable def classicalPointHomeomorph (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ≃ₜ
      Set.range (fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
        classicalPoint x a.1 a.2) :=
  (isEmbedding_classicalPoint x).toHomeomorph

@[simp]
theorem coe_classicalPointHomeomorph_apply (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K))
    (a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}) :
    (classicalPointHomeomorph x a : closedPolydisc n K) = classicalPoint x a.1 a.2 :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The subspace of classical evaluation points in `closedPolydisc n K` is a Baire space** in its
induced topology: it is homeomorphic to the complete metric space `(K°)ⁿ`. -/
instance baireSpace_range_classicalPoint (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    BaireSpace (Set.range fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      classicalPoint x a.1 a.2) :=
  (classicalPointHomeomorph x).isOpenQuotientMap.baireSpace

/-! ### Closedness of the rational points over locally compact base fields -/

/-- **When `K°` is compact, the classical `K`-rational points form a closed subset of
`closedPolydisc n K`.** Around any point `v` outside the range, for each `a ∈ (K°)ⁿ` some
coordinate difference `Tᵢ - aᵢ` lies outside `v.supp`, so continuity of `v` furnishes a basic open
`|ϖᵐ| ≤ |Tᵢ - aᵢ| ≠ 0` containing `v` and excluding an open ball around `a` in `(K°)ⁿ`; compactness
of `(K°)ⁿ` reduces these exclusions to finitely many. -/
theorem isClosed_range_classicalPoint_of_compactSpace [CompactSpace (powerBoundedSubring K)]
    (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    IsClosed (Set.range fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      classicalPoint x a.1 a.2) := by
  classical
  have hcomp : CompactSpace {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} :=
    (powerBoundedTupleHomeomorph n K).symm.compactSpace
  rw [← isOpen_compl_iff, isOpen_iff_mem_nhds]
  intro v hv
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ₀, hϖ₁⟩ := NormedField.exists_norm_lt_one K
  have hϖNil : IsTopologicallyNilpotent ϖ := tendsto_pow_atTop_nhds_zero_of_norm_lt_one hϖ₁
  choose idx exp hmem using fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
    exists_mem_basicOpen_weightedX_sub_weightedC_of_ne_classicalPoint
      (fun h ↦ hv ⟨a, h.symm⟩) hϖNil
  let B (a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)}) :
      Set {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} :=
    {b | ‖b.1 (idx a) - a.1 (idx a)‖ < ‖ϖ ^ exp a‖}
  have hBopen (a) : IsOpen (B a) :=
    isOpen_lt (((continuous_apply (idx a)).comp continuous_subtype_val).sub continuous_const).norm
      continuous_const
  have haB (a) : a ∈ B a := by
    simpa [B] using pow_pos hϖ₀ (exp a)
  obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover B hBopen
    fun a _ ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨a, haB a⟩
  let W : Set (closedPolydisc n K) :=
    ⋂ a ∈ S, Subtype.val ⁻¹' basicOpen
      (weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (ϖ ^ exp a))
      (weightedX _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (idx a) -
        weightedC _ isWeightFamily_one_weight (a.1 (idx a)))
  have hWopen : IsOpen W :=
    S.finite_toSet.isOpen_biInter fun a _ ↦
      (isOpen_basicOpen _ _).preimage continuous_subtype_val
  have hvW : v ∈ W := Set.mem_biInter fun a _ ↦ hmem a
  refine Filter.mem_of_superset (hWopen.mem_nhds hvW) ?_
  rintro w hw ⟨b, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨a, haS, hbB⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hS (Set.mem_univ b))
  have hw' := Set.mem_iInter₂.mp hw a haS
  simp only [Set.mem_preimage, mem_basicOpen_iff, classicalPoint_vle, map_sub,
    evalAtHom_weightedC, evalAtHom_weightedX, vle_iff_norm_le_of_mem_spa x.2] at hw'
  exact hw'.1.not_gt hbB

/-- Over a proper nontrivially normed ultrametric field `K` (such as `ℚ_[p]` or any finite
extension), the classical `K`-rational points form a closed subset of `closedPolydisc n K`. -/
theorem isClosed_range_classicalPoint_of_properSpace [ProperSpace K]
    (x : spa (powerBoundedSubring K)) :
    IsClosed (Set.range fun a : {a : Fin n → K // ∀ i, IsPowerBounded (a i)} ↦
      classicalPoint x a.1 a.2) :=
  isClosed_range_classicalPoint_of_compactSpace x

end Embedding

